{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"b6c7d248-cfaa-49e7-8b8f-01684d4b8588","outcome":{"verdict":"escalation","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/command-registry-handler-extraction/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/__tests__/architecture-ratchet.test.ts","title":"Ratchet Check 3 uses line-split regex instead of @typescript-eslint/parser (design spec deviation)","rationale":"design.md D4 and tasks.md T-17 explicitly require @typescript-eslint/parser for AST-based ImportDeclaration analysis. The implementation uses comment-stripped newline-split text search. A multi-line import whose `from \"command-registry\"` clause is on a different line from the `import {` keyword would silently evade the check, defeating the ratchet for that pattern. The design requirement states: 'AST 等の構造検査を優先し、コメントや文字列で誤検知する単純 grep だけに依存しないこと'.","line":107},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/scaffold-handlers.ts","title":"Uses ctx!.invokerCwd instead of process.cwd() as specified in tasks.md T-14 and TC-023","rationale":"tasks.md T-14 and test-case TC-023 specify process.cwd() as the CWD argument for executeRulesNew and executeReviewersNew. The original inline handlers in command-registry.ts (main branch) used process.cwd(). The extracted handlers use ctx!.invokerCwd. usage-handler.ts has the same substitution. The requirement '意味を変えずに移動する' (move without changing meaning) is technically violated. In practice ctx.invokerCwd equals process.cwd() at dispatch time, making the substitution functionally equivalent but undocumented. TC-023 asserts process.cwd() is used, but no automated test verifies the argument value.","line":14},{"severity":"low","resolution":"decision-needed","file":"bin/specrunner.ts","title":"Duck-type error guards added outside R3a scope (pure code movement constraint)","rationale":"R3a is scoped to 'コードの純粋な移動と依存整理に限定する'. bin/specrunner.ts introduces isFlagParseError and isSpecRunnerError duck-type guards that replace strict instanceof checks. The duck-type guards accept any Error with a matching .name (and exitCode property for SpecRunnerError), which is semantically broader than instanceof. This is outside the declared scope and is a minor behavior change in edge cases (e.g. an Error from an unrelated module with name === 'FlagParseError').","line":12,"options":[{"label":"Accept as companion fix","consequence":"The handler extraction exposes instanceof brittleness under Vitest resetModules. Accepting documents the fix and keeps the branch self-consistent. Add a note to the PR about the out-of-scope companion change."},{"label":"Defer to separate PR","consequence":"Revert the duck-type guard changes from this PR. Address in a dedicated follow-up. Requires verifying no test failures are introduced by the revert."}]}],"evidence":{"checked":25,"skipped":0,"unverified":2},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/cli/command-registry.ts","title":"ARCHIVE_USAGE is both imported and re-exported in the same file","rationale":"Line 25 imports ARCHIVE_USAGE from ./archive.js for use on line 856 (help.detail). Line 26 re-exports it for backward compatibility. This double-declaration is intentional per design.md D3 and works correctly, but may look surprising to future readers."},{"severity":"low","file":"src/cli/__tests__/architecture-ratchet.test.ts","title":"Ratchet Check 3 correctly excludes __tests__/ subdirectory via readdirSync non-recursion","rationale":"fs.readdirSync(CLI_DIR) returns only direct entries; the __tests__ directory name is filtered by the .endsWith('.ts') check. Test files that legitimately import from command-registry are correctly excluded from the ratchet. This is correct behavior."}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":1}},"startedAt":"2026-09-02T16:31:38.107Z","endedAt":"2026-09-02T16:38:42.137Z","commitOid":